LOCALE(1)                   User Commands                  LOCALE(1)

NAME
    locale - print locale information

SYNOPSIS
    locale [-a]
    locale [-k] keyword...

DESCRIPTION
    locale prints the locale of each category that LANG, LC_ALL and the
    LC_* variables select, the installed locales, or the values of locale
    keywords. The locales are the files in /usr/share/i18n/locales.

OPTIONS
    -a   list the installed locales
    -k   print each keyword with its name

KEYWORDS
    codeset, decimal_point, thousands_sep, d_t_fmt, d_fmt, t_fmt,
    t_fmt_ampm, date_fmt, am_pm, day, abday, mon, abmon, alt_mon,
    yesexpr, noexpr, crncystr

EXAMPLES
    LANG=fr_FR.UTF-8 locale
    LANG=ru_RU.UTF-8 locale -k mon

SEE ALSO
    date(1), index(7)
